+"""Tiered routing in the worker: preflight, range parsing with cache, quality check, merge and hand-off (D-15, D-53, D-56).
+
+One run parses a document range by range at the tier the preflight chose. Every finished range is cached under the
+tenant's parse-cache prefix, so a reclaimed job converts nothing twice (D-56). The ranges are merged in page order into
+one Docling document, turned into the ParseResult the app's post-parse stages read, cached as the ``merged`` entry and
+handed to ``advance``. A dry run stops after the checks and writes no document (D-33).
+
+CPU work (preflight, conversion, merge, chunking) runs in the priority pool when the worker has one; backfill ranges
+are cut into sub-ranges so an upload can take the pool between them (A-4). Logs and errors carry job id, pages and
+reason codes only; no document text.
+"""
 
